📊 Kickstarter Crowdfunding Dashboard (Power BI)
📌 Project Overview

This project presents an interactive Kickstarter Crowdfunding Dashboard built using Power BI to analyze project performance, funding trends, and success rates across different categories, countries, and time periods.

The goal of this project is to transform raw crowdfunding data into meaningful insights that help understand:

What makes a project successful
Which categories perform best
Funding patterns over time
🎯 Objective
Analyze crowdfunding trends over the years
Identify top-performing projects and categories
Compare successful vs failed projects
Track funding performance across countries
Enable interactive filtering for deeper insights
📂 Dataset
Source: Kickstarter dataset (public dataset)
Data includes:
Project Name
Category & Subcategory
Country
Goal Amount
Pledged Amount
Backers Count
Launch Date & Deadline
Project Status (Successful/Failed)
📊 Dashboard Features
🔢 Key KPIs
💰 Total Funds Raised: 3.86 Billion
👥 Total Backers: 44.52 Million
✅ Successful Projects: 140.3K
💸 Total Amount Pledged: 4.76 Billion
📦 Total Projects: 365.9K
🎯 Total Goal: 18.38 Billion
📈 Visualizations
Top 10 Projects by Pledged Amount
Highlights highest funded projects
Helps identify successful campaign patterns
Top Projects by Country
Shows geographical distribution of projects
US dominates crowdfunding activity
Total Pledged by Category & State
Compares successful vs failed projects across categories
Total Projects by Year & Quarter
Time-series analysis of project trends
Peak observed around 2014–2016
Category Distribution (Tree Map)
Film & Video, Publishing, Music lead the market
🎛️ Filters & Interactivity
📅 Quarter Filter (Q1–Q4)
🌍 Country Filter
📆 Year Slider

These filters allow users to dynamically explore the data and gain customized insights.

🛠️ Tools & Technologies
Power BI
Data Cleaning & Transformation (Power Query)
DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)
Data Visualization Techniques
📌 Key Insights
🎬 Film & Video and Publishing are top-performing categories
🇺🇸 Majority of projects come from the United States
📉 Many projects fail to meet their funding goals
📈 Rapid growth observed between 2012–2015
💡 Successful projects tend to have higher backer engagement
🚀 How to Use
Open the .pbix file in Power BI Desktop
Use filters (Quarter, Year, Country)
Hover over visuals for detailed insights
Analyze trends and patterns interactively
